  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $\\phi=4 t^{2}+6 x+9$ and $t=2 \\mathrm{s}$ We know that $\\varepsilon=\\frac{d \\phi}{d t}$\r\nHere, $\\frac{d \\phi}{d t}=8 t+6$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n\\left(\\frac{d \\phi}{d t}\\right)_{t=2} &=8 \\times 2+6 \\\\\r\n\\varepsilon &=22 \\mathrm{V}\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
